      "amount": "1/2 cup",
      "notes": "thinly sliced"
    },
    {
      "name": "olive oil",
      "amount": "2 tbsp"
    },
    {
      "name": "salt",
      "amount": "to taste"
    },
    {
      "name": "pepper",
      "amount": "to taste"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat a panini press or grill to medium-high heat.",
    "Butter one side of each bread slice.",
    "Place one slice of bread, butter-side down, in the panini press.",
    "Top with a slice of provolone cheese, a few slices of pickle, some arugula, cherry tomatoes, and red onion.",
    "Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper.",
    "Place another slice of bread, butter-side up, on top of the filling.",
    "Close the panini press and cook for 3-4 minutes, or until the bread is golden brown and the cheese is melted.",
    "Repeat with the remaining ingredients.",
    "Cut the sandwiches in half and serve immediately."
  ],
